  "id": "hougoumont",
  "title": "Hougoumont",
  "date": "18 June 1815, late morning",
  "blurb": "Prince Jérôme's division is sent to draw Wellington's reserves onto the walled farm of Hougoumont, out in front of the Allied right. A thick wood screens the buildings from the south; behind it stand a loopholed garden wall, an orchard ringed with hedges, and a hollow way running back up to the Guards on the ridge. It was meant to be a feint. It became a battle of its own.",
  "hint": "The wood hides you from the farm until you come out thirty yards from the loopholed garden wall. Clear the wood first, work round by the orchard or the Nivelles road, and cut the hollow way that feeds the garrison from the ridge.",
